# Explanations

## Performance

The most high-performing Felsenstein's likelihood calculator
implementations in both [BEAGLE][b] (used by BEAST X and BEAST2) and
`b3` are the GPU ones, both powered by CUDA.  `b3` includes a number of
optimizations which allow it to outperform BEAGLE on the largest and the
most computationally demanding datasets.

- [Kernel count optimization][kc]


[b]: https://beagle-dev.github.io/
[kc]: /explanation/kernels
